WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.221
Mental models are internal representations of how a system, task, or situation works.

2
00:00:05.221 --> 00:00:10.443
They help performers interpret what they see and decide what to do next.

3
00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:24.099
A strong mental model connects parts into a working picture: what is normal, what is unusual, which signals are meaningful, what failure modes are plausible, and which actions are likely to change the outcome.

4
00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:30.123
Situational awareness is the practical ability to notice, interpret, and update understanding of relevant conditions.

5
00:00:30.123 --> 00:00:32.935
It is not memorizing every possible detail.

6
00:00:32.935 --> 00:00:40.165
It is knowing what matters right now, what has changed, what is uncertain, and what may happen next.

7
00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:46.591
Expert performers filter noise more effectively because their mental models help them recognize meaningful cues earlier.

8
00:00:46.591 --> 00:00:49.804
This is one reason experts can appear fast.

9
00:00:49.804 --> 00:00:52.214
They are not always skipping analysis.

10
00:00:52.214 --> 00:00:56.632
Often they are using organized knowledge to narrow the problem quickly.

11
00:00:56.632 --> 00:01:03.460
They notice a cue, connect it to a pattern, check a constraint, and anticipate the next risk.

12
00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.476
That speed is useful when it is grounded in evidence.

13
00:01:07.476 --> 00:01:13.501
It becomes dangerous if the performer stops updating when new information contradicts the first pattern.

14
00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:15.509
Strong performance requires active updating.

15
00:01:15.509 --> 00:01:19.526
Assumptions should be treated as working hypotheses, not permanent facts.

16
00:01:19.526 --> 00:01:28.764
When the environment changes, expert performers ask what no longer fits, what signal is missing, and what evidence would cause a different decision.

17
00:01:28.764 --> 00:01:31.575
Situational awareness is not a static snapshot.

18
00:01:31.575 --> 00:01:36.395
It is a living model that gets revised as the work unfolds.
